      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the prime factorization method. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of each number:**\n   - The prime factorization of 12 is \\(12 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 = 2^2 \\times 3\\).\n   - The prime factorization of 20 is \\(20 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 5 = 2^2 \\times 5\\).\n\n2. **Identify the common prime factors:**\n   - The common prime factor between 12 and 20 is \\(2\\).\n   - The lowest power of the common prime factor \\(2\\) in the factorizations is \\(2^2 = 4\\).\n\n3. **Multiply the common prime factors with their lowest powers to find the GCD:**\n   - The GCD is \\(2^2 = 4\\).\n\nTherefore, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).\n\nThe Soccer Master's in a league had 200 players this season. 40 players quit at the end of the first half season while the rest played the second half season. The soccer master recruited 2 times the number of players who quit in the first half. What is the final count of players in the league?\n\n1. Determine the number of players who left after the first half season:\n   - ( text{first_half_leavers} = text{first_half_players} times text{first_half_leavers_factor} )\n\n2. Calculate the number of players remaining after the first half:\n   - ( text{first_half_remaining} = text{first_half_players} - text{first_half_leavers} )\n\n3. Compute the number of players added after the first half:\n   - ( text{added_players} = text{added_factor} times text{first_half_leavers} )\n\n4. Determine the total number of players after the second half:\n   - ( text{final_players} = text{first_half_remaining} + text{added_players} )\n\nThe final number of players in the soccer league after the second half season is ( text{final_players} ). This value is the answer.\n\nIn summary, the steps and calculations are as follows:\n- Number of players who left after the first half: ( 200 times 0.2 = 40 )\n- Players remaining after the first half: ( 200 - 40 = 160 )\n- Players added after the first half: ( 0.2 times 40 = 8 )\n- Total number of players after the second half: ( 160 + 8 = 168 )\n\nThus, the total number of players in the soccer league after the second half season is ( 168 ).\n\nThe answer is ( 168 ).",
