      "text": "To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 12 and 20, we can use the prime factorization method:\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of 12:**\n   - 12 can be divided by 2: \\(12 \\div 2 = 6\\)\n   - 6 can be divided by 2: \\(6 \\div 2 = 3\\)\n   - 3 is a prime number.\n   So, the prime factorization of 12 is \\(2^2 \\times 3\\).\n\n2. **Prime Factorization of 20:**\n   - 20 can be divided by 2: \\(20 \\div 2 = 10\\)\n   - 10 can be divided by 2: \\(10 \\div 2 = 5\\)\n   - 5 is a prime number.\n   So, the prime factorization of 20 is \\(2^2 \\times 5\\).\n\n3. **Identify Common Prime Factors:**\n   - The prime factors of 12 are \\(2^2 \\times 3\\).\n   - The prime factors of 20 are \\(2^2 \\times 5\\).\n   - The common prime factors are \\(2^2\\).\n\n4. **Calculate the GCD:**\n   - The GCD is the product of the lowest powers of all common prime factors.\n   - The common prime factor \\(2^2\\) can be written as \\(2 \\times 2\\).\n   - Therefore, the GCD of 12 and 20 is \\(2 \\times 2 = 4\\).\n\nThus, the greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
